"""A surface-form approximation to an early word-fragment feature.

The negative response is strongest for a long vowel-initial lowercase
fragment following a one-letter word beginning, especially a capital.
It is weaker at a bare word boundary or after two letters. Ordinary
productive suffixes are exempt. Short URL host fragments lean positive.
Three recurrent rare-name pieces (as in Folland, Gaskell and Riesel)
have a much stronger negative response near a word's beginning. Familiar
Holland, Haskell and diesel completions are exempted from that boost.
This is only a partial approximation of the remaining lexical variation.
