"""Layer-0 MLP down-projection component 3946: a subject pronoun fused with its predicate.

What it does: it fires on a single token that is a subject (I, you, he, she, it, or the
Japanese 私, Korean 나는/내가) joined to the verb, adverb or auxiliary that starts the
predicate, e.g. 我说, 他认为, 你可以, 我们将, 我不是, 私は. In those tokens the clause's
verb is due next. Such tokens get a large activation (about 6).

What it does not do: the bare pronoun (我, 我们, 他们) and the pronoun plus a possessive or
noun (我的, 他的, 我国, 他人) stay near 0 or weak. Demonstrative and person-noun subjects
that begin a predicate (这是, 这就, 人都, 人是) get a moderate value. English reflexives
(himself, themselves, itself) get a small value. Everything else is 0.

The program reads only the newest token, so it needs no carry state.
"""

